  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Food Insecurity at the Time of Climate Change: Sharing and Learning from Bottom-Up Responses in the Caribbean Region</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Research network across the greater Caribbean to address food insecurity. The primary benefiting countries involved are Colombia, Jamaica, Belize and Antigua &amp; Barbuda (until 2022). Develop best practice model for local &amp; emergency conditions. Benefiting local partner organisations &amp; multi-disciplinary learning. SDGS: 2,17,13</narrative>
  </description>
  <description type="2">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">The Global Challenges Research Fund (GCRF) supports cutting-edge research to address challenges faced by developing countries. The fund addresses the UN sustainable development goals. It aims to maximise the impact of research and innovation to improve lives and opportunity in the developing world.</narrative>
  </description>
